      {
        "detail": "",
        "id": "goal",
        "kind": "goal",
        "ref": null,
        "title": "Let independent implementation agents resume the right venture, claim bounded work, return source-backed results and report friction without losing context or silently widening scope."
      },
      {
        "detail": "",
        "id": "research",
        "kind": "record",
        "ref": {
          "id": "b5d3b837-2d7f-41ec-9b20-7b19e9e3bcd6",
          "kind": "work"
        },
        "title": "MVP scope and evidence review"
      },
      {
        "detail": "",
        "id": "pilot",
        "kind": "question",
        "ref": null,
        "title": "Does the completed MVP help in repeated real use?"
      },
      {
        "detail": "",
        "id": "expand",
        "kind": "alternative",
        "ref": null,
        "title": "Extend only the demonstrated useful workflow"
      },
      {
        "detail": "",
        "id": "revise",
        "kind": "alternative",
        "ref": null,
        "title": "Narrow or use an existing tool if reuse/benefit fails"
      },
      {
        "detail": "Use prepared configs and maps; one writer per venture at a time, parallelism across venture repositories. Verify claim, prepare, result preview/accept, resume and feedback receipt. No production model service.\nAcceptance: Every prepared repo resolves its own workspace and current work; stale/conflicting claims fail; failed feedback send is retained and retry is idempotent.\nProposed package: materialize only after prerequisite acceptance.",
        "id": "F01",
        "kind": "alternative",
        "ref": null,
        "title": "F01: Run one complete agent handoff per venture"
      },
      {
        "detail": "Inspect Foundry unreviewed feedback evidence plus local outboxes. Reproduce highest-impact issue, classify duplicate/accepted/deferred/rejected with rationale and link a bounded Foundry work item; do not treat every suggestion as mandatory.\nAcceptance: At least one completed real venture package can be resumed by a fresh agent without reading full chat; retained feedback has decision and work reference or explicit defer reason.\nProposed package: materialize only after prerequisite acceptance.",
        "id": "F02",
        "kind": "alternative",
        "ref": null,
        "title": "F02: Triage observed agent friction"
      },
      {
        "detail": "Measure time to identify work, context bytes, omitted information, stale submissions and manual recovery. Fix concrete recurring cases with regression tests. Keep provider/action/storage boundaries replaceable.\nAcceptance: No source lost in context; changed evidence invalidates unsafe effects; completed work is absent from executable queue; app remains useful without the helper.\nProposed package: materialize only after prerequisite acceptance.",
        "id": "F03",
        "kind": "alternative",
        "ref": null,
        "title": "F03: Improve context and queue behavior only where measured"
      },
      {
        "detail": "Run standalone lint/types/product/agent-kit/browser/container checks appropriate to changes, installed CLI and backup/restore. Update direction and one operator guide; preserve exact evidence IDs.\nAcceptance: A clean checkout supports two separate venture agents and later review; no unconfigured external actions, no claimed commercial or token savings without measurement.\nProposed package: materialize only after prerequisite acceptance.",
        "id": "F04",
        "kind": "alternative",
        "ref": null,
        "title": "F04: Release the dogfood-supported local MVP update"
      },
